messages:
maria: Quick sync — we need SDK + docs alignment for the "unified API" launch next quarter. Main bullets: structured output schema, function/tool-calling surface, embeddings vs rerank contract, and TS/Python type changes. Propose a code freeze for API surface in 3 weeks and migration guides. What are the breaking risk vectors?
ajay: Agree we should avoid breaking call signatures where possible. Plan: add optional `structured_output` and `tool_calls` fields rather than renaming params. For TS we'll bump major if types export changes, but runtime can accept old props via a small compat layer. Timeline: compat layer + tests by next Wed, types PR by Fri.
sam: Docs notes — we need short migration examples (2-3 snippets) showing old->new for chat and completions, an embeddings vs rerank decision matrix, and a changelog entry with code diffs. Also we should update quickstarts and the examples repo. I'll draft examples once SDK PR lands.
ajay: Quick example (TS) of the proposed optional structured output type:
```ts
export type StructuredField = { name: string; type: 'string'|'number'|'object' };
export type StructuredSpec = { schemaId?: string; fields?: StructuredField[] };
export interface ChatRequestV2 {
  model: string;
  input: string;
  structured_output?: StructuredSpec;
  tool_calls?: Array<{ name: string; args: Record<string, unknown> }>;
}
```
Runtime will accept ChatRequestV1 | ChatRequestV2 using a normalizeRequest helper.
lia-devex-bot: Created a deck slide and added checklist item: "SDK compat layer" -> assigned to ajay; PR template updated with "migration examples" checkbox. Link: https://tiny.redwood/docs/ride
maria: OK — triage time. Owners: ajay = SDK compat + types, sam = docs/examples/changelog, maria = launch criteria + customer comms. Deliverables: SDK PR (compat) by next Wed, docs draft by next Fri, internal beta with partners 2 weeks after that. If blockers surface we postpone feature gate. :thumbsup:
ajay: Sounds good — will post a minimal PR today for review and include the normalizeRequest helper + unit tests.
sam: I'll sketch three short examples tonight and link them to the PR.
maria: Thanks everyone — will coordinate customer asks and post a short RFC in #product tomorrow.
